WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.621 --> 00:00:16.222
be sorry to leave Mr.

2
00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:19.943
Hobbs," Cedric told his mother at breakfast the next morning.

3
00:00:19.963 --> 00:00:24.845
"I'll miss all my friends, but especially him.

4
00:00:25.626 --> 00:00:26.706
And he'll miss me."

5
00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:30.448
"I understand, Cedric," Mrs.

6
00:00:30.568 --> 00:00:31.168
Errol said.

7
00:00:32.256 --> 00:00:40.778
"I'll miss my friends and Mary and this little house Her voice trailed off, and a tear rolled

8
00:00:40.878 --> 00:00:41.759
down her cheek.

9
00:00:43.779 --> 00:00:45.840
Cedric got up and gave her a hug.

10
00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:49.141
"We'll manage, Mama."

11
00:00:51.381 --> 00:00:55.082
As soon as the grocery store opened, Cedric went to see Mr.

12
00:00:55.122 --> 00:00:58.403
Hobbs. "Good morning!"

13
00:00:58.963 --> 00:01:01.604
the grocer said, setting aside his newspaper.

14
00:01:02.988 --> 00:01:06.049
"Hello," Cedric said mournfully.

15
00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:12.531
He didn't climb onto his usual stool but stood with his hands in his pockets.

16
00:01:13.931 --> 00:01:16.172
He dreaded breaking the news to his friend.

17
00:01:16.192 --> 00:01:21.273
"Mr. Hobbs, do you remember what we were talking about yesterday?"

18
00:01:21.613 --> 00:01:22.334
Cedric said.

19
00:01:22.354 --> 00:01:24.994
"Hmm," Mr.

20
00:01:25.034 --> 00:01:25.734
Hobbs said.

21
00:01:25.754 --> 00:01:28.675
"I think it was England."

22
00:01:30.376 --> 00:01:35.727
"Yes, but when Mary arrived what were we discussing then?"

23
00:01:36.327 --> 00:01:37.247
Cedric asked.

24
00:01:37.267 --> 00:01:39.929
"Let's see."

25
00:01:40.969 --> 00:01:42.710
Mr. Hobbs rubbed his chin.

26
00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:47.053
"Queen Victoria and the aristocracy."

27
00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:49.674
"And earls.

28
00:01:50.254 --> 00:01:56.098
You said you wouldn't have any earls sitting around here, wearing their robes and coronets."

29
00:01:56.118 --> 00:01:58.499
"That's right!"

30
00:01:58.999 --> 00:02:00.020
Mr. Hobbs said.

31
00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.021
"And I called them tyrants too!"

32
00:02:03.041 --> 00:02:06.242
"I forgot that part."

33
00:02:07.323 --> 00:02:11.484
Cedric turned bright red with embarrassment as he took a seat on a barrel.

34
00:02:11.504 --> 00:02:13.625
"Well, Mr.

35
00:02:13.685 --> 00:02:17.247
Hobbs, an earl is sitting here right now."

36
00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:21.168
The grocer almost jumped out of his chair.

37
00:02:21.188 --> 00:02:29.792
"What?" "Yes, I am an earl—or rather I'm going to be one."

38
00:02:31.624 --> 00:02:34.627
Mr. Hobbs hurried to check the thermometer in the front window.

39
00:02:38.189 --> 00:02:41.112
a hot day, and the heat has gone to your head.

40
00:02:42.413 --> 00:02:43.273
How do you feel?"

41
00:02:43.774 --> 00:02:45.675
Mr. Hobbs asked with concern.

42
00:02:45.695 --> 00:02:48.157
"Do you hurt anywhere?"

43
00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.082
He laid his hand on Cedric's forehead.

44
00:02:54.102 --> 00:02:57.765
"Poor Cedric," he thought.

45
00:02:57.785 --> 00:03:01.208
"Something is very wrong with him today!"

46
00:03:02.956 --> 00:03:05.797
"Thank you, but I'm all right," Cedric said.

47
00:03:05.817 --> 00:03:10.158
"I'm just sorry to say I'm really going to be an earl.

48
00:03:11.118 --> 00:03:12.659
That's why Mary fetched me.

49
00:03:14.379 --> 00:03:18.320
The earl's lawyer traveled all the way from England to tell my mother."

50
00:03:20.161 --> 00:03:24.022
Mr. Hobbs sank into his chair and mopped his face with his handkerchief.

51
00:03:24.042 --> 00:03:26.963
"One of us has heatstroke!"

52
00:03:28.703 --> 00:03:30.324
"No, we're both fine.

53
00:03:31.328 --> 00:03:33.470
Now let me tell you what the lawyer said."

54
00:03:35.131 --> 00:03:40.154
Mr. Hobbs listened carefully as Cedric told the story of how he became Lord Fauntleroy.

55
00:03:41.275 --> 00:03:45.799
When Cedric finished, the grocer asked, "Who's your grandfather?"

56
00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.421
Cedric pulled a paper from his pocket.

57
00:03:49.441 --> 00:03:53.604
"I wrote down his name because I couldn't remember it all.

58
00:03:54.665 --> 00:03:58.608
John Arthur Molyneux Errol, Earl of Dorincourt.

59
00:04:01.752 --> 00:04:05.373
And that's who I'll be someday, the Earl of Dorincourt."

60
00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:09.754
Mr. Hobbs let out a low whistle.

61
00:04:12.815 --> 00:04:14.676
"What did you say your name is now?"

62
00:04:14.696 --> 00:04:17.377
"Lord Fauntleroy."

63
00:04:18.857 --> 00:04:20.578
Mr. Hobbs looked amazed.

64
00:04:20.598 --> 00:04:23.358
"Well, isn't that something!"

65
00:04:23.378 --> 00:04:27.440
"England is very far away, isn't it?"

66
00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:28.640
Cedric said.

67
00:04:29.856 --> 00:04:31.037
"Oh my, yes.

68
00:04:31.377 --> 00:04:33.238
It's across the Atlantic Ocean."

69
00:04:33.258 --> 00:04:37.100
"That's the worst part," Cedric said.

70
00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:41.342
"I probably won't see you for a long time."

71
00:04:43.924 --> 00:04:47.666
The two friends sat quietly for a few minutes, thinking about that.

72
00:04:49.127 --> 00:04:49.867
Finally Mr.

73
00:04:49.907 --> 00:04:50.647
Hobbs spoke.

74
00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:54.109
"Are you sure you have to be an earl?"

75
00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:57.251
Cedric nodded sadly.

76
00:04:57.271 --> 00:04:58.852
"I'm sure.

77
00:04:59.356 --> 00:05:02.517
All I can do is try to be a good one."

78
00:05:04.898 --> 00:05:07.218
Cedric spent a long time talking to Mr.

79
00:05:07.258 --> 00:05:13.320
Hobbs. On his way home, he saw some of his friends.

80
00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.781
They were taking turns racing against each other.

81
00:05:16.801 --> 00:05:19.822
"Come on, Cedric!"

82
00:05:20.262 --> 00:05:21.142
one boy called.

83
00:05:21.162 --> 00:05:22.963
"Join us!

84
00:05:23.303 --> 00:05:26.104
You can race Billy to the lamppost by your house."

85
00:05:27.604 --> 00:05:31.746
Cedric quickly forgot about being an earl and joined Billy at the starting line.

86
00:05:33.186 --> 00:05:34.867
At just this moment, Mr.

87
00:05:34.907 --> 00:05:37.388
Havisham's carriage pulled into Cedric's street.

88
00:05:39.629 --> 00:05:43.351
Mr. Havisham signaled for the driver to stop so he could watch the race.

89
00:05:44.671 --> 00:05:46.512
"Ready, set, go!"

90
00:05:47.052 --> 00:05:49.694
the first boy called, and the racers took off.

91
00:05:49.714 --> 00:05:52.915
"Come on, Lord Fauntleroy!"

92
00:05:53.415 --> 00:05:55.116
Mr. Havisham said quietly.

93
00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:02.104
Cedric ran as fast as he could and touched the lamppost two seconds before Billy.

94
00:06:02.124 --> 00:06:06.047
"Bravo, Lord Fauntleroy!"

95
00:06:06.527 --> 00:06:09.029
Mr. Havisham said more loudly this time.

96
00:06:09.049 --> 00:06:12.152
"Three cheers for Cedric!"

97
00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:15.174
the boys cried, surrounding their friend.

98
00:06:16.615 --> 00:06:19.798
Cedric noticed Billy standing off to the side by himself.

99
00:06:19.818 --> 00:06:22.921
"Hey, Billy, come here!"

100
00:06:24.862 --> 00:06:26.904
The winner put his arm around the loser.

101
00:06:27.884 --> 00:06:29.285
"You know why you lost, Billy?

102
00:06:30.185 --> 00:06:30.785
It's simple.

103
00:06:31.226 --> 00:06:34.747
My legs are longer than yours, and I'm three days older than you.

104
00:06:36.308 --> 00:06:38.209
That gave me a huge advantage."

105
00:06:40.129 --> 00:06:41.730
Billy slowly smiled.

106
00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:45.852
"Yes, Cedric, I'm sure you're right."

107
00:06:48.393 --> 00:06:51.074
Mr. Havisham's smile turned into a frown.

108
00:06:51.094 --> 00:06:55.256
"Cedric is such a kind boy," he thought.

109
00:06:56.484 --> 00:06:59.268
"It's a pity he has to live with the earl.

110
00:07:00.489 --> 00:07:04.213
He has no idea how hard that will be."

111
00:07:05.695 --> 00:07:07.938
There was something else Cedric didn't know yet.

112
00:07:09.379 --> 00:07:13.104
When he moved to England, he'd be living apart from his mother.
